-{"id":"QA-OFF-BY-ONE-61","title":"[P3] bunker-qa lockstep test is red on an unmodified harness (10 stale/lost assertions) — new harness regressions are indistinguishable from baseline noise","status":"pending","priority":"P3","complexity":3,"type":"qa-harness","created_by":"foreman","source":"foreman-audit","created_at":"2026-11-03T20:30:00Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T20:30:00Z","attempts":0,"capability_tags":["qa-harness","test-drift","lockstep"],"depends_on":[],"blocks":[],"reasoning":"MEASURED 2026-11-03 (tick off-by-one-foreman-2026-11-03-19-51-49) while closing QA-OFF-BY-ONE-15-R2. `bash /home/kara/.hermes/scripts/test_bunker_qa_classifier.sh` on an UNMODIFIED harness reported 'RESULT: 44 passed, 13 failed'. After the R2 fix it reports 'RESULT: 54 passed, 10 failed' — the ten remaining FAILs are pre-existing and unrelated to R2, so they were deliberately left untouched rather than widened into that row's scope fence.\n\nThe ten (verbatim FAIL descriptions):\n  1. chaos-disconnect vacuous/0-byte gate present: expected yes got no\n  2. chaos-disconnect 0-byte UNVERIFIED branch present: expected yes got no\n  3. behavioral: could extract the disc chain: expected yes got no\n  4. discovery prefers long-running commands: expected yes got no\n  5. generated battery: run is a second-pass fallback: expected yes got no\n  6. Docker lifecycle cells default disabled: expected yes got no\n  7. both Compose lifecycle cells pass through safety gate: expected yes got no\n  8. active gateway and persistent Hermes bind mount are guarded: expected yes got no\n  9. live controller hard-block overrides an inherited opt-in: expected yes got no\n 10. invalid lifecycle flag is rejected: expected yes got no\n\nWHY IT MATTERS: a lockstep suite that is red before anyone touches the harness cannot distinguish a NEW harness regression from baseline noise — the next QA row that adds a guard reads 'it was already failing', and a real loss (like the QA-CHIMERA-V2-42 CLI-help arm R2 had to restore) hides inside the count. Either the harness lost those guards (re-adopt them, as R2 did for the banner arm) or the assertions are stale (replace them with assertions the live harness satisfies and record the owning row).","acceptance_criteria":"`bash /home/kara/.hermes/scripts/test_bunker_qa_classifier.sh` exits 0 with `RESULT: N passed, 0 failed` on the live harness, reached one of two ways for EACH of the ten named assertions: (a) the harness is fixed and the assertion passes as written, or (b) the assertion is rewritten to pin behaviour the live harness actually has, with the owning row id in a comment above it. No assertion may be deleted without a comment naming why it is obsolete. REJECTS: raising the baseline count, marking failures 'known' without a harness-side reason, or editing the test so it no longer drives the RENDERED script.","detail":"Reproduce: bash /home/kara/.hermes/scripts/test_bunker_qa_classifier.sh; read the FAIL lines at the bottom.","exit_code":null,"files_changed":[],"lines_added":0,"lines_removed":0,"commit_hash":null,"completed_at":null,"guard_result":null,"judge":null,"worker_status":"pending","worker_summary":null,"foreman_note":"Filed by the foreman tick that closed QA-OFF-BY-ONE-15-R2 (2026-11-03). Deliberately NOT fixed in that row: its scope fence was the Go start-probe false green, and folding ten unrelated lockstep drifts in would have made the fix unjudgeable.","ci_result":null}
