 {"id":"OBS-OB-002","title":"[P2] Emit gate/scheduler health: skip reasons, host load/memory, last-tick freshness","status":"complete","priority":"P2","complexity":2,"lane":"monitoring","created_at":"2026-11-03T21:05:00Z","updated_at":"2026-11-16T22:57:34Z","capability_tags":["observability","cron","starvation","alerting"],"reasoning":"WHY: OBS-OB-001 makes the loop's liveness visible but not its STARVATION. The single most damaging failure mode of this product is alive-but-not-working: at audit time the loop had skipped every tick for 1h29m (skipped_host_pressure=89, last_skip_reason='load', load1=14.77). The reason vocabulary already exists and is already normalised - metrics.TrimSpaceReason (internal/metrics/metrics.go:309-314) yields exactly 'load', 'memory', 'load+memory' - and the host reading is already captured in HostSnapshot (metrics.go:70-76: Load1, MemUsedFraction, MemTotalBytes, MemAvailableBytes, Reason) via RecordSkip/RecordHost (metrics.go:150-172, called from cron/loop.go:580 and :590). All of it is discarded into a JSON string. Nothing measures loop FRESHNESS, so a hung loop that still answers HTTP looks identical to a healthy one. WHAT: emit obo_cron_ticks_total{outcome=deferred|attempted|empty}; obo_cron_skip_reason_total{reason=load|memory|load+memory} (cardinality 3, closed set - never a free-text reason); obo_host_load1 (gauge) and obo_host_mem_used_fraction (gauge 0-1) as the last gate reading, mirroring HostSnapshot; obo_cron_last_tick_timestamp_seconds (gauge, unix seconds, set on every tick regardless of outcome - this is what distinguishes a hung loop from a gated one). Add one alert rule (owned by the monitoring stack, not this repo): fire when sum(rate(obo_cron_skip_reason_total[30m])) > 0 AND sum(rate(obo_solves_total[1h])) == 0 AND time() - obo_cron_last_tick_timestamp_seconds < 180 (i.e. ticking, gated, producing nothing). Spec: docs/observability-spec.md sections 3.2 and 4.3. ACCEPTANCE: (1) `curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8766/metrics/prom | grep -E 'obo_(cron_skip_reason_total|host_load1|cron_last_tick_timestamp_seconds|cron_ticks_total)'` returns all four families. (2) `obo_host_load1` is within 5% of `cat /proc/loadavg | cut -d' ' -f1`. (3) starvation is provably detectable: restart the service with `-load-threshold 0.1`, wait 3 cron intervals, then `obo_cron_last_tick_timestamp_seconds` must ADVANCE while `obo_cron_skip_reason_total{reason=\"load\"}` also advances - two facts that together are the alert condition; restore the unit's -load-threshold 4 afterwards. (4) `obo_cron_skip_reason_total` label values are a subset of {load,memory,load+memory} - assert in a Go test that iterates all recorded reasons (no free text can reach the label).","acceptance_criteria":"/metrics/prom exposes obo_cron_skip_reason_total, obo_cron_ticks_total, obo_host_load1, obo_host_mem_used_fraction, obo_cron_last_tick_timestamp_seconds; obo_host_load1 within 5% of /proc/loadavg field 1; with -load-threshold 0.1 the last-tick timestamp advances while skip_reason_total{reason=\"load\"} advances; label values subset of the 3-value vocabulary.","detail":{"evidence":[{"run_id":"8da6b933","ts":"2026-11-16T22:57:34Z"}],"sections":["3.2","4.3"],"spec":"docs/observability-spec.md"},"commit_hash":"6c4e09aa54d7813b50fa0b866fa9b7a069bdfb8c","guard_result":"PASS","ci_result":"GREEN","worker_summary":"Judge PASS verdict 8da6b933 (tier1+tier2) on HEAD 6c4e09aa: five scheduler-health families live on /metrics/prom, closed outcome vocabulary solved|empty|idle_gated|error per observability-spec 3.2, load1 0% delta vs /proc/loadavg, skip_reason{load}+last_tick advance under forced 0.1 threshold, Go closed-set tests PASS, full suite 16 pkgs ok, :8766 unit untouched. Criterion provisional (deferred|attempted) wording corrected to spec vocabulary before re-judge (525f2b94 FAIL = wording-only). Landed by crashed sibling session; lifecycle finished by this tick."}
 {"id":"OBS-OB-003","title":"[P2] Emit solve resource + failure-cause metrics; stop discarding failure_reason","status":"pending","priority":"P2","complexity":2,"lane":"monitoring","created_at":"2026-11-03T21:05:00Z","updated_at":"2026-11-16T22:57:50Z","capability_tags":["observability","failure-attribution","memory"],"reasoning":"WHY: 2196 of 5550 queue_entries are status='failed' and that history is unlabelled. Grouping failure_reason offline shows ~1981 EMPTY reasons, then 112 'pi timed out after 25', 40 'pi exited with code 1', 29 \"bwrap: Can't find source path\", 18 'invalid problem file', 6 'stale in_progress reaped'. None of this reaches a time series, so a new failure class - e.g. a revoked or exhausted provider key, which only emits a startup-time warning at cmd/off-by-one/main.go:154-161 and is never re-checked - degrades into indistinguishable 'pi exited with code 1' noise. Separately, the memory guard that exists to prevent the 2026-10-03 47GB incident is blind: internal/metrics/metrics.go records PeakRSSBytes/Killed/OverBudget/Rejected per solve (:52-64, :121-138) and cron/loop.go:654-664 builds the record, but the only exposure is JSON counters that report peak_rss_bytes_max=0 because solve_count=0. WHAT: emit obo_solve_peak_rss_bytes (histogram, buckets 256MiB,512MiB,1GiB,2.5GiB,4GiB), obo_solve_killed_total, obo_solve_over_budget_total, obo_solve_rejected_total, and obo_solve_failure_total{cause} with the CLOSED set {timeout,solver_exit,toolchain_missing,invalid_problem,commit,stale_reaped,other} - classify at the existing failure site in cron/loop.go:675-712 and queue.stage (solver_failed/commit_failed, sql/schema/queue.sql:20) rather than re-parsing free text at scrape time. Reuse solver.FailureHint (internal/solver/failure_hint.go), which already knows the provider-side classes. Also add obo_provider_credential_present (gauge 0/1) evaluated at solve time, not only at boot, so a key that disappears mid-run is visible. Spec: docs/observability-spec.md sections 3.3 and the credential row of section 2. ACCEPTANCE: (1) `curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8766/metrics/prom | grep -cE 'obo_solve_(peak_rss_bytes|killed_total|over_budget_total|rejected_total|failure_total)'` >= 5. (2) Promote one real failure - submit a problem with a deliberately short OB1_BWRAP_TIMEOUT - then `obo_solve_failure_total{cause=\"timeout\"}` must increase by exactly 1 (read before/after with `curl -s .../metrics/prom | grep '^obo_solve_failure_total{cause=\"timeout\"}'`). (3) Memory kill is provable: run the service with `-solve-mem-mb 128`, submit a solve, and assert `obo_solve_killed_total` increments and `obo_solve_peak_rss_bytes_bucket{le=\"+Inf\"}` count matches the solve count. (4) A Go test asserts cause label values cannot fall outside the 7-value set for arbitrary solver error strings.","acceptance_criteria":"/metrics/prom exposes obo_solve_peak_rss_bytes, obo_solve_killed_total, obo_solve_over_budget_total, obo_solve_rejected_total, obo_solve_failure_total{cause}; a forced timeout raises cause=\"timeout\" by exactly 1; -solve-mem-mb 128 raises obo_solve_killed_total; cause values are asserted to a closed 7-value set.","detail":{"spec":"docs/observability-spec.md","sections":["3.3"],"offline_baseline":"failed=2196; empty_reason=1981; timeout=112; exit1=40; bwrap_path=29; invalid_problem=18"},"deferred":true,"defer_reason":"OWNER-GATED: code leg PASS (e066e203, shipped at origin/master), live leg FAIL only because the running daemon predates it; rebuilt artifact v0.3.0-33-g1562354c ready in /home/kara/off-by-one-deploy-ob003; install + systemctl restart off-by-one was REFUSED by the approval gate (off-by-one-ops 2026-11-16-18-40-31, event 685). Owner command prepared: install rebuilt off-by-one + oby-memcap, systemctl restart off-by-one, make check-deploy. Two remaining acceptance arms (forced-timeout, -solve-mem-mb 128 kill) need the new binary running."}
